From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:55:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1185/3799] soh: rename func_8006907C ->
 Cutscene_ClearUnusedFlag

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: clears gUnusedCsFlag when it is set, and nothing else; nothing anywhere calls it.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_demo.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_demo.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_demo.c b/soh/src/code/z_demo.c
index 22aa4dccb..971009cb4 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_demo.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_demo.c
@@ -2211,7 +2211,8 @@ void Cutscene_InitUnusedState(PlayState* play) {
     D_8015FCE4 = 0;
 }
 
-void func_8006907C(PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_8006907C: clears gUnusedCsFlag when it is set, and nothing else; nothing anywhere calls it.
+void Cutscene_ClearUnusedFlag(PlayState* play) {
     if (D_8015FCCC != 0) {
         D_8015FCCC = 0;
     }
